{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And to teach, He gave, etc.</b> The meaning is that since there are many wise men whose wisdom remains in their heart alone, not knowing how to teach it, therefore it says <b>He put in his heart to teach</b> — He granted him the wisdom of instruction. Further, it comes to exclude what is written in Yoma 38a, that the House of Garmu did not wish to teach about the making of the showbread, the House of Avtinas did not wish to, and so forth; and the verse informs us that concerning such people the saying applies (Proverbs 10:7) ״זֵכֶר צַדִּיק לִבְרָכָה״ — but these, by contrast, would instruct and teach all who wished."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:59.515859906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}